#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:1
msgid "Decision not to use Nix in the Codespace environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:3
msgid "Status: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:4
msgid "Date: 2026-09-19"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:5
msgid "Decision-makers: tkoyama010"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:7
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:9
msgid "[ADR-0013](0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md) adopts a GitHub Codespaces devcontainer for developing pyvista-wasm with the pi coding agent. That devcontainer must install Python (via uv), Node.js (via npm), and pre-commit with all hooks. [Nix](https://nixos.org/) (including [devenv](https://devenv.sh/) and [devbox](https://www.jetify.com/devbox)) can define the whole toolchain declaratively and reproducibly, and Nix-based devcontainer features exist for Codespaces. Should the Codespace environment be built with Nix instead of the plain devcontainer features CI already uses?"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:11
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:13
msgid "**Reproducibility**: the pi agent should always see the exact tool versions CI sees."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:14
msgid "**Single source of truth**: the repository already pins its toolchain in `uv.lock` and `package-lock.json`; a second, parallel pin format invites drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:15
msgid "**Maintenance cost**: pyvista-wasm is a small project; every extra tool in the environment definition is a real ongoing cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:16
msgid "**Onboarding friction**: contributors and the pi agent must be able to start without learning a new package manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:17
msgid "**CI parity**: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) promises CI verifies the environment on every PR; the Codespace should reuse the CI install steps, not fork them."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:19
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:21
msgid "**Option A: Use Nix (devenv/devbox) to define the Codespace environment**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:22
msgid "**Option B: Use plain devcontainer features with uv and npm (status quo)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:24
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:26
msgid "Chosen option: \"**Option B: Use plain devcontainer features with uv and npm (status quo)**\", because the lockfiles CI already enforces give the reproducibility Nix would provide, without adding a second package manager to maintain."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:28
msgid "Reproducibility is already covered: `uv.lock`, `package-lock.json`, and pinned pre-commit hook revisions pin every tool version. Nix would pin them a second time in a second format."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:29
msgid "CI runs `uv`, `npm`, and `pre-commit` directly. A Nix-based environment replaces those entry points with Nix wrappers, so the Codespace and CI would diverge in *how* they run the same tools — the exact drift ADR-0013's confirmation step is meant to catch."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:30
msgid "Nix adds a learning curve for every contributor who debugs the environment, and Nix builds inside Codespaces need care (the store lives outside the container filesystem, caches are non-trivial)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:31
msgid "The project has no packages to distribute and no need for hermetic builds beyond what the lockfiles and CI already provide."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:33
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:35
msgid "Good, because the Codespace reuses the CI install steps verbatim; one source of truth per toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:36
msgid "Good, because no contributor needs to learn Nix to fix the environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:37
msgid "Good, because Codespace image builds stay simple and fast."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:38
msgid "Bad, because byte-identical environments across machines are not guaranteed the way a Nix store would guarantee them; platform differences (glibc, shell) can still leak in."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:39
msgid "Bad, because if the project later needs hermetic, multi-language pinning beyond lockfiles (e.g. system-level native dependencies for VTK/WASM builds), this decision should be revisited."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:41
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:43
msgid "Compliance is confirmed by the absence of Nix files (`flake.nix`, `devenv.nix`, `devbox.json`, `default.nix`) and by the devcontainer installing its toolchain through uv/npm features or the same steps CI runs. If a Nix definition appears under `.devcontainer/` or the repository root without a superseding ADR, this decision is violated."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:45
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:47
msgid "Option A: Use Nix (devenv/devbox) to define the Codespace environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:49
msgid "Nix (possibly via devenv or devbox) defines Python, Node.js, and pre-commit in one declarative, content-addressed environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:51
msgid "Good, because environments become byte-for-byte reproducible across machines and over time."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:52
msgid "Good, because one declarative file could replace per-manager lockfiles as the single pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:53
msgid "Bad, because it duplicates pinning: `uv.lock` and `package-lock.json` would still exist for CI and local use."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:54
msgid "Bad, because Nix adds a package manager, a language, and a cache layer that every maintainer must understand."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:55
msgid "Bad, because CI does not run Nix today; adopting it in the Codespace forks the environment definition from CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:57
msgid "Option B: Use plain devcontainer features with uv and npm (status quo)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:59
msgid "The devcontainer installs the toolchain with the same commands CI uses, backed by the existing lockfiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:61
msgid "Good, because lockfiles and pinned hook revisions already pin tool versions; reproducibility is adequate."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:62
msgid "Good, because Codespace, local, and CI environments run identical commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:63
msgid "Good, because nothing new to learn or maintain beyond the devcontainer file itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:64
msgid "Neutral, because system-level dependencies beyond uv/npm's reach would need ad-hoc Dockerfile lines if they ever appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:65
msgid "Bad, because cross-platform reproducibility is not bit-exact the way Nix provides."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:67
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:69
msgid "Prerequisite decision: [ADR-0013 — Decision to add a pi coding agent development environment to GitHub Codespaces](0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:70
msgid "Toolchain pins: `uv.lock`, `package-lock.json`, and the pinned revisions in [`.pre-commit-config.yaml`](../../.pre-commit-config.yaml)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md:71
msgid "Revisit triggers: a need for hermetic system-level dependencies (e.g. native toolchains for the VTK/WASM build) that uv and npm cannot pin, or repeated environment drift between Codespace and CI."
msgstr ""
